The probability that two adjacent points are of different colors is: $$
\mathbb{P}(\text{one red, one blue}) = 2 \cdot \frac{n}{n + k} \cdot \frac{k}{n + k} = \frac{2nk}{(n + k)^2}
$$

$$
\mathbb{E}[X] = (n + k) \cdot \frac{2nk}{(n + k)^2} = \frac{2nk}{n + k}
$$

$$
\mathbb{E}[m] = \mathbb{E}[X] = \boxed{\frac{2nk}{n + k}}
$$

### ✅ Final Answer: $$
\boxed{\mathbb{E}[m] = \frac{2nk}{n + k}}
$$
